    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1181">

                <pb facs="1186" n="1020" sameAs="frus:frus1917/pg1020"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 812.504/82</note>
                <head ana="#head_untitled-inferred-from-preceding-sibling-head">[Untitled]</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1917-04-25T17:00:00-05:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">April 25, 1917, 5 p.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>131. Consul Dawson telegraphs striking employees of Eagle Oil Company yesterday
                    assaulted with weapons American official of company. Manager of company,
                    presumably British, was also assaulted. Authorities, although advised of
                    threats, took no precautions, and did not act until British Consul demanded
                    protection and arrest of rioters. Consul has been informed strikers have
                    received anonymous contribution of five hundred American dollars. More serious
                    situation expected May 1.</p>
                <p>Take up with appropriate authorities, and request that definite instructions be
                    telegraphed to Tampico officials to take immediate steps to protect American
                    life and property.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Lansing</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
